                                "sense_id": "109d0905-7ce0-399a-9775-87d7dd900b5a",
                                "text": "[…] Claggart's unobserved glance happened to light on belted Billy rolling along the upper gun deck in the leisure of the second dog-watch, exchanging passing broadsides of fun with other young promenaders in the crowd […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "49ffd200-9f4a-4763-85bc-5f935b8a6097",
                                "sense_id": "109d0905-7ce0-399a-9775-87d7dd900b5a",
                                "text": "When Bournemouth began laying track, it splashed onto the scene in style, launching two in 1908 with the East Cliff and West Cliff Lifts. Both connected promenaders with the beach, at extreme ends of the town."
